PRE-TABLE BLOCK, PASS 13 -- the GPT-6 Astra fix review (2026-09-04) read the contract's enumeration against the
handler and found it false for five arms; the main loop re-derived every finding from the tree before this file.
(mtime against part13/driver.log is the order witness.)

  - SIBLING PARITY -- the five HUH?-testing arms (VECBASE ~0xf0, SCCICR/SCCTX ~0x1f, SCCRX/SCSIICR ~0xdf) were
    enumerated as having NO `if'; their sibling TxCTL has its HUH? partition held both ways (0x0004 clear /
    0x0008 set) and TxICR too (0x0000 / 0x0020).  The asymmetry is five open HUH?-CLEAR cells: every wide
    value the rows drive at the five (0x0303, 0xaab8, lanes 0xdd/0x44/0xb8) has bits outside the mask.
  - CLAIM -> ROW -- "INT clear with a count pending is UNREACHABLE": REFUTED by reading pcc_timer_tick()
    (increments the count from the host timer, no reassert) and DEVICE_TICK (reasserts): the cell exists in
    the window between them.  Not constructible by a probe -> DISCLOSED, no row.  Its converse, INT SET
    with count 0: CONSTRUCTIBLE (an IEN-clear byte write zeroes the count; only ICLR clears INT; reassert
    only sets it) -> a floor cell under both argued bounds -> ROWED at both labels.
  - GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the TxICR body reads reg&INT and pending_timerN together in its ICLR arm
    (`(idata & ICLR) && reg & INT && pending > 0'); the pass-11 enumeration treated INT as derived from the
    count.  They DISAGREE after an IEN-clear write (count 0, INT set) -- the third state no row built.
  - CHANNEL -- rbq <arm> <- M_HUH<arm> (readback: the landed masked value vs the preset; 0xf0/0x50, 0x10/0x1f,
    0x01/0x1f); pend2 rbz <- M_ZINT2 (0x33 vs 0x23); pend1 rbz <- M_ZINT1 (0x33 vs 0x23); the zctl rows are
    controls (byte writes; no mutant here lands or declines a byte write) and are predicted GREEN everywhere.

PREDICTIONS for part 13 (seven mutants plus BASE, 251-row instrument; each mutant conditions ONE arm's guard):
    BASE            251/251
    M_HUHV          250/251   rbq vecbase 0xf0 (mask 0xf0 stores the whole lane)
    M_HUHSI         250/251   rbq sccicr 0x10
    M_HUHST         250/251   rbq scctx 0x10
    M_HUHSR         250/251   rbq sccrx 0x1
    M_HUHSS         250/251   rbq scsiicr 0x1
    M_ZINT2         250/251   pend2 rbz 0x33 (IEN lands; reassert does not set INT at count 0 and INT was already set)
    M_ZINT1         250/251   pend1 rbz 0x33
  Order effects: none expected -- every new write is the LAST in its session, so nothing reads after it.
  A prediction that misses in the SAFE direction (extra reds) is recorded, not repaired; one that misses in the
  UNSAFE direction (a predicted red that stays green) is a mis-built row or mutant and stops the round.
